  <data name="Info_Bars_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Progress bars</value></data>
  <data name="Info_Bars_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>MegaCopier has three bars: the total one (how much of the whole copy is left), the one for the file being copied and the small ones in the copy list. Each can have its own style.\nChoose which one to change at the top, tap a style and adjust the details. The preview shows how it looks while copying, paused, with an error and when finished.\n• A striking bar (Neon, Fire, Rainbow) to see progress at a glance from across the room.\n• A subtle one (Thin line, Fluent) if you work while copying and want no distractions.\n• Traffic light to know without reading numbers whether there is a lot or a little left.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarColors_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Colors</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_ColorsDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>The theme’s, your own, traffic light or rainbow.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarColors_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Where the bar’s colors come from.\n• From the theme: they change by themselves when you pick another theme.\n• My colors: a gradient with the two colors you choose (tap a swatch or the Start / End button).\n• Traffic light: red at the start, amber halfway and green at the end; you know how much is left without reading the number.\n• Rainbow: every color.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarThickness_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Thickness</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_ThicknessDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>How tall the bar is.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarThickness_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The height of the bar in pixels. &quot;From the theme&quot; uses the chosen theme’s.\n• Thicker: easier to see from afar and looks better in styles like Wave, Fire or Pixels.\n• Thinner: more subtle, ideal with Thin line or on small screens.\nIf you put the percentage inside, the bar grows just enough to read it.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarRadius_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Rounding</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_RadiusDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Square or rounded corners.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarRadius_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>How round the ends of the bar are. 0 leaves square corners, like classic bars; the maximum turns it into a pill. &quot;From the theme&quot; uses the theme’s rounding.\n• Square: look great with Blocks, Pixels and Terminal.\n• Round: softer and more modern, perfect with Fluent, Neon or Glass.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarSpeed_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Effect speed</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_SpeedDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>How fast shines, waves and stripes move.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarSpeed_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Changes the pace of the bar’s animations, not the copy speed. 1× is normal; 0.25× is very slow and 3× very fast.\n• Slower: more relaxed, ideal if the bar is always in view.\n• Faster: feels busier and catches the eye.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarGlow_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Shine and glow</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_GlowDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>How intense reflections and light are.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarGlow_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Raises or lowers how intense the shines are: the Aero reflection, the Neon glow, the Comet head, the bubbles or the Metal glint.\n• At 0%: the bar is flat and sober.\n• At 100%: it shines at full; ideal with dark themes.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarText_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Percentage</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_TextDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>On the right, inside the bar or hidden.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarText_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Where the percentage number is shown.\n• On the right: as always, outside the bar.\n• Inside the bar: the number sits on top of the fill and the bar grows so it can be read; leaves more room for other details.\n• Hidden: just the bar, for a cleaner look (the percentage is still in the window title).</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarMotion_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>How it moves</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_MotionDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Smooth, elastic or in steps.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarMotion_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>How the fill moves each time the copy advances.\n• Smooth: glides with no jerks (recommended).\n• Elastic: overshoots a touch and comes back, like a spring; more playful.\n• In steps: moves 5% at a time, like the bars of old; looks great with Blocks or Pixels.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarEffects_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>State effects</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_EffectsDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stripes when paused, a shake on error and a flash when done.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarEffects_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The bar tells you what is happening without reading anything.\n• Paused: still amber stripes appear.\n• On an error: it turns red and gives a small shake.\n• When finished: a green celebration flash (on the total bar and in the list).\nTurn it off if you prefer a bar that only changes color.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarBorder_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Border</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_BorderDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>A thin line around the bar.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarBorder_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Draws a thin line around the bar so it stands out from the background.\n• Useful with light or textured themes, where the empty track is barely visible.\n• Looks great with Glass and Outline.</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarReduce_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Reduce animations</value></data>
  <data name="Bars_ReduceDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Still bars, with no repeating effects (for all of them).</value></data>
  <data name="Info_BarReduce_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Removes repeating motion (shines, waves, stripes, blinking). The bar still advances normally.\n• Useful if animations distract you or make you dizzy.\n• Saves a little battery on laptops.\nIt also turns on by itself if you turn off &quot;Animation effects&quot; in Windows (Settings &gt; Accessibility &gt; Visual effects).</value></data>
