  <data name="Info_SameDrive_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>New copies while another one is running</value></data>
  <data name="Info_SameDrive_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>When you copy something while another copy is running, MegaCopier looks at which drive it&apos;s going to.\n• To the same drive: by default it asks. “Add it” puts its files at the end of the running copy&apos;s list (each in its own folder), with a single bar. “Separate copy, afterwards” leaves it waiting its turn. “At the same time” copies both together, but both get slower.\n• To another drive: it starts right away, because each drive writes at its own speed. If you&apos;d rather it wait its turn, change it here.\nExample: you copy a movie to a USB stick and then another folder to the same stick: MegaCopier comes to the front and you decide. If meanwhile you copy something to drive D:, it starts without waiting.</value></data>
  <data name="Settings_CloseButtonTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>When you click the window&apos;s X</value></data>
  <data name="Settings_CloseButtonDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>By default it cancels the copies, like “Stop” on each one. MegaCopier stays in the tray for the next copy.</value></data>
